+# Revealing a source occurrence
+
+GitHub flavor on iOS and Android accepts a transient Find highlight without
+changing the user's text selection or copy behavior. Rebuild the native client
+after updating the package.
+
+Pass `sourceDocumentRevision` as a document revision string and `sourceSelection`
+as `{version: 1, revision, requestId, sourceMarkdown, ranges}`. `sourceMarkdown`
+must equal the exact `markdown` prop. Each range is `{start, end}` in UTF-16,
+end-exclusive. Use separate ranges across Markdown syntax. Source entities,
+escaped characters and normalized newlines are atomic, so include their complete
+source interval. The renderer rejects partial, stale or unmapped selections.
+
+For a generated pill label, supply `labels` entries shaped as
+`{kind: 'link-label', sourceStart, sourceEnd, text, start, end}`. The source
+anchor is the minimum source start and maximum source end of the link label's
+parsed text runs, or the full auto-recognized link. Formatting delimiters outside
+those runs are excluded. `text` must equal the actual pill
+label. `start` and `end` index that label in UTF-16. A pill is one attachment,
+so selecting part of its label highlights the whole pill.
+
+Use `sourceLinkPillContent={[{sourceStart, sourceEnd, label}]}` to give separate
+uses of one URL different labels. These labels take precedence over URL labels
+and retain the configured icon and style. They require `sourceDocumentRevision`.
+
+`onSourceSelection` receives a native event containing
+`{version: 1, revision, requestId, status, rects}`. An applied result contains
+glyph or attachment rectangles in renderer-root coordinates after horizontal
+code and table scrolling. Use them to scroll the surrounding feed vertically.
+A rejected result has no rectangles. Match request and revision before using
+the result. The wrapper also ignores stale events. Layout changes may report
+new rectangles for the same request.
+
+Set `sourceSelection` to `null` to clear the highlight. Clearing and recycled
+views do not emit a result. CommonMark and web do not implement this API.
